  {
    "path": "packages/runtime-vapor/src/components/KeepAlive.ts",
    "from_line": 336,
    "to_line": 372,
    "why": "Vapor KeepAlive's onBeforeUnmount iterates each cached branch and decides its fate: the current branch is deactivated (kept, with its da hook queued), every other cached branch is detached into the storage container via remove(), and all kept-alive EffectScopes are stopped."
  },
  {
    "path": "packages/runtime-core/src/components/KeepAlive.ts",
    "from_line": 239,
    "to_line": 253,
    "why": "VDOM KeepAlive's onBeforeUnmount decides per cached vnode: the current one keeps its keep-alive flag reset and only gets its deactivated hook queued, while every other cached entry is unmounted outright."
  },
  {
    "path": "packages/runtime-core/src/components/KeepAlive.ts",
    "from_line": 168,
    "to_line": 172,
    "why": "The local unmount() helper resets the component's COMPONENT_SHOULD_KEEP_ALIVE shape flag and calls the raw unmount so a cached branch can be removed outright instead of deactivated."
  },
  {
    "path": "packages/runtime-core/src/renderer.ts",
    "from_line": 2413,
    "to_line": 2424,
    "why": "The generic component unmount path checks COMPONENT_SHOULD_KEEP_ALIVE and short-circuits to deactivation (keep) via the KeepAlive context instead of actually unmounting the component."
  }
]
```

Based on my analysis, the decision lives in the `onBeforeUnmount` handlers of both KeepAlive implementations, plus the cache-pruning helper.

